      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ❌ **Changes Requested** — Blocking issues found in `common/peripheral_charger.c` and `zephyr/test/drivers/pchg/src/main.c`; see inline comments.\n\n### Review Summary\n- **Functionality**: Correctly replaces `sizeof(event_names)` and `sizeof(state_names)` with `ARRAY_SIZE(event_names)` and `ARRAY_SIZE(state_names)` in `_text_event()` and `_text_state()` so out-of-bounds enum values return `\"UNDEF\"` instead of reading past the pointer arrays.\n- **Architecture \u0026 Component Fit**: In `zephyr/test/drivers/Kconfig`, `config LINK_TEST_SUITE_PCHG` should be placed before `source \"Kconfig.zephyr\"`. In `zephyr/test/drivers/testcase.yaml`, using the existing `common` tag and inline `extra_configs` avoids adding a bespoke `peripheral_charger` tag to `util/twister_tags.py` and a separate `pchg/prj.conf`.\n- **Code Simplicity**: In `common/peripheral_charger.c`, prefer marking `_text_event()` and `_text_state()` with `test_export_static` (from `include/common.h`) rather than adding `#ifdef CONFIG_ZTEST` pass-through wrapper functions (`test_text_event()` and `test_text_state()`).\n- **Idiomaticity \u0026 Readability**: Using `test_export_static` matches existing `common/` conventions across the repository.\n- **Security**: Fixes an out-of-bounds array read when logging or formatting invalid `enum pchg_event` or `enum pchg_state` values.\n- **Testing**: In `zephyr/test/drivers/pchg/src/main.c`, `zassert_not_null()` on valid inputs is vacuous because out-of-bounds inputs also return a non-null string (`\"UNDEF\"`); tests should assert the exact returned string and cover the lower bound (`0`), upper valid bound (`COUNT - 1`), and adjacent out-of-bounds values (`COUNT`, `COUNT + 1`, `-1`).\n- **CL Size \u0026 Scope**: `Size: M (+78, -2)` — Appropriately scoped to the bounds check fix and its unit test.\n- **Commit Message**: Clear explanation of the bug (byte size vs. element count of pointer arrays) and the fix.\n\n[[trajectory](https:/