      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] Two test coverage and assertion issues in these bounds tests:\n\n1. **Vacuous assertion for valid inputs (`zassert_not_null`)**: Because `_text_event()` and `_text_state()` return `\"UNDEF\"` (a non-null string literal) for out-of-bounds inputs, `zassert_not_null(...)` will pass even if the function returns `\"UNDEF\"` or the wrong entry name. Assert the exact returned string with `strcmp(...) \u003d\u003d 0`.\n2. **Missing boundary cases (`0`, `COUNT - 1`, `COUNT + 1`, and negative values)**: To thoroughly verify the `\u003c ARRAY_SIZE(...)` bounds check without arbitrary magic offsets (`+ 10`), test the lower boundary (`0`), the last valid element (`PCHG_EVENT_COUNT - 1` / `PCHG_STATE_COUNT - 1`), the exact upper boundary (`COUNT`), the adjacent out-of-bounds value (`COUNT + 1`), and `-1`:\n\n```c\nZTEST(pchg, test_text_event_bounds)\n{\n\t/* Valid boundary events (first and last valid indices) */\n\tzassert_equal(0, strcmp(\"NONE\", _text_event(PCHG_EVENT_NONE)));\n\tzassert_equal(0,\n\t\t      strcmp(\"INITIALIZED\", _text_event(PCHG_EVENT_INITIALIZED)));\n\tzassert_equal(0, strcmp(\"UPDATE_ERROR\",\n\t\t\t\t_text_event(PCHG_EVENT_UPDATE_ERROR)));\n\n\t/* Out-of-bounds events */\n\tzassert_equal(0, strcmp(\"UNDEF\", _text_event((enum pchg_event)-1)));\n\tzassert_equal(0, strcmp(\"UNDEF\", _text_event(PCHG_EVENT_COUNT)));\n\tzassert_equal(0, strcmp(\"UNDEF\", _text_event(PCHG_EVENT_COUNT + 1)));\n}\n\nZTEST(pchg, test_text_state_bounds)\n{\n\t/* Valid boundary states (first and last valid indices) */\n\tzassert_equal(0, strcmp(\"RESET\", _text_state(PCHG_STATE_RESET)));\n\tzassert_equal(0, strcmp(\"BIST\", _text_state(PCHG_STATE_BIST)));\n\n\t/* Out-of-bounds states */\n\tzassert_equal(0, strcmp(\"UNDEF\", _text_state((enum pchg_state)-1)));\n\tzassert_equal(0, strcmp(\"UNDEF\", _text_state(PCHG_STATE_COUNT)));\n\tzassert_equal(0, strcmp(\"UNDEF\", _text_state(PCHG_STATE_COUNT + 1)));\n}\n```\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/9000d1ca-6bef-40dd-ab48-1e4532742e86)",
